3;margin:0 0 15px"><span>France, of course, is no stranger to social unrest=
=2E During the yellow-vest protests that raged between 2018 and 2020, tens =
of thousands of people, wearing high-visibility safety vests, turned out fo=
r weekly demonstrations that also began as a protest against rising fuel pr=
ices, then grew into demands for political and economic justice.</span></p>=
<p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"=
><span>President Emmanuel Macron =E2=80=94 perhaps mindful of the potential=
 similarities between then and today =E2=80=94 last Thursday chaired a meet=
ing of leaders of the G7 industrialized countries, in which they agreed to =
release 100 million barrels of diesel and crude oil from their stockpiles t=
o ease pressure on fuel prices. He said he hoped the emergency measure woul=
d cause prices to =E2=80=9Cdrop at the pump as quickly as possible.=E2=80=
=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;ma=
rgin:0 0 15px"><span>But energy prices are only one source of pressure.</sp=
an></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 =
0 15px"><span>The country=E2=80=99s fiscal jitters have been amplified by r=
ecent polls that show the far-right candidate, Marine Le Pen, is on track t=
o beat all her rivals in presidential elections next spring.</span></p><p s=
tyle=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><sp=
an>Her victory is far from preordained. She has been convicted of financial=
 corruption, which she denies, and her party president, Jordan Bardella, ha=
s been accused of antisemitism, which he also denies. In a runoff against a=
 centrist, Le Pen might still lose, analysts say.</span></p><p style=3D"fon=
t:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>But in a=
nother scenario, the double whammy of economic problems and social unrest c=
ould play to the advantage of political extremes on both right and left. Th=
at scenario could send Le Pen into a runoff against a far-left candidate. A=
nd in that situation, analysts say, she=E2=80=99d likely prevail.</span></p=
><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px=
"><span>What would a Le Pen victory mean for France=E2=80=99s ability to st=
ay afloat=3F On Tuesday, she unveiled her economic agenda and promised to r=
educe government spending by 140 billion euros by 2032. (Though, given the =
students marching outside, she also promised to protect spending on educati=
on.)</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;m=
